<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jebe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1223</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jebe was one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>'s leading generals. A warrior of the Besud clan serving the Taichiud, he wounded Temüjin with an arrow in battle and was then taken into his service. In 1218 he conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-khitai">Qara Khitai</a> and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuchlug">Kuchlug</a>, and with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subutai">Subutai</a> he pursued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmshah">Khwarazmshah</a> Muhammad II across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, then raided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> and the steppe, defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgians">Georgians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumans">Cumans</a> and Rus' at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalka">Kalka</a> River in 1223.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>This strength proved brittle: the Mongol vanguard of <b>Jebe</b> and Subutai defeated George IV at Khunan in 1221, and the Khwarazmian ruler Jalal al-Din sacked Tbilisi in 1226.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-georgia">Kingdom of Georgia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…the Khwarazmian Empire (1219–1221) demonstrated mastery of logistics, reconnaissance and psychological warfare, while generals such as Subutai and <b>Jebe</b> defeated the Rus and Kipchaks at the Kalka River in 1223, and Subutai later led the western campaign that devastated the Rus principalities and defeated Polish and Hungarian armies…</blockquote><a href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1216 Genghis sent <b>Jebe</b> against Kuchlug, who fled and in 1218 was captured and decapitated; the Mongols completed the conquest in 1220.</blockquote><a href="/empire/qara-khitai">Qara Khitai · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The Mongols under <b>Jebe</b> and Subutai took Shamakhi in 1221, and from the 1230s Shirvan was subject to Mongol rule.</blockquote><a href="/empire/shirvanshah-state">Shirvanshah State · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1223 the Bulgars ambushed and defeated part of the Mongol army of Subutai and <b>Jebe</b> near the Samara Bend as it returned from the Battle of the Kalka River.</blockquote><a href="/empire/volga-bulgaria">Volga Bulgaria · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Genghis Khan promoted men for loyalty and ability rather than birth: <b>Jebe</b>, who according to the Secret History of the Mongols had once shot the khan’s horse from under him in battle, became one of his leading generals.</blockquote><a href="/government/nomadic-confederation">Nomadic confederation · Strengths</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=46,105&amp;year=1213" aria-label="Mongolia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7032 544 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Jebe"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7482 814h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7482 814h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=46,105&amp;year=1213">What was here in 1213? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
